      "text": "Now the main design task — `guardrails.py`. My design rationale:\n\n- **Schema isolation**: the agent owns `staging`/`reference`; reads allowed anywhere, but writes/drops/grants outside owned schemas (e.g. the reporting team's `reporting`) are refused.\n- **Dangerous calls**: `db.drop_table` and `db.grant` need human approval even in owned schemas (irreversible / privilege-changing).\n- **Tasks**: routine work (loads, backfills, transformations, data-quality, maintenance, notifications) starts immediately; warehouse reconfigurations and uncategorised requests require approval.\n- **Allowlist**: unknown tools denied; optional domain allowlist for URL tools.\n\nI'm deliberately avoiding imports from sibling modules (there's no `__init__.py`, so modules may be loaded standalone):",
